WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.383 --> 00:00:05.363
Two routes feed one gracile neuron.

2
00:00:06.323 --> 00:00:07.703
How can you tell what each one carries?

3
00:00:08.817 --> 00:00:12.117
Take one route away at a time, and watch what the neuron loses.

4
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:19.020
Turecek, Lehnert and Ginty recorded single gracile neurons in the hindlimb region of

5
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.500
anaesthetized adult mice.

6
00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:24.570
They identified neurons that project to the thalamus.

7
00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:29.730
Stimulating their axons there sent spikes backward, checked with a collision test.

8
00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.090
Switch one removes the direct route.

9
00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:43.130
Light on the gracile nucleus silences the afferent terminals there, through a

10
00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:44.590
light-gated chloride channel.

11
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.840
Switch two removes the indirect route.

12
00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.300
Drugs on the lumbar cord block its spinal synapses.

13
00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:56.740
The afferents’ direct branches climb past without a spinal synapse, so they keep

14
00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:57.740
conducting.

15
00:00:58.283 --> 00:01:00.243
Then three stimuli on the hindpaw.

16
00:01:01.183 --> 00:01:04.363
A vibration. A gentle displacement of the skin.

17
00:01:05.183 --> 00:01:07.023
And a sustained press with a blunt probe.

18
00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:09.253
Pause and predict.

19
00:01:10.253 --> 00:01:11.553
Which route carries vibration?

20
00:01:12.373 --> 00:01:14.193
Which carries a hard, sustained press?

21
00:01:15.013 --> 00:01:16.133
And gentle displacement?

22
00:01:22.233 --> 00:01:28.233
Vibration first. The direct input carried vibration with high temporal precision, up

23
00:01:28.233 --> 00:01:29.233
to high frequencies.

24
00:01:30.153 --> 00:01:33.113
The indirect route can add to slow, 10 hertz vibration.

25
00:01:36.317 --> 00:01:42.457
Now the press. Blocking the spinal synapses almost eliminated sustained firing in

26
00:01:42.457 --> 00:01:43.457
most neurons.

27
00:01:44.117 --> 00:01:47.997
The block also raised the force needed to make the neuron fire at all.

28
00:01:48.737 --> 00:01:51.317
So the indirect route is not just a late add-on.

29
00:01:54.267 --> 00:01:56.467
Gentle displacement used both routes.

30
00:01:57.367 --> 00:02:00.767
So direct for vibration, indirect for light touch, is too simple.

31
00:02:04.367 --> 00:02:07.467
Now map each input's receptive field on one neuron.

32
00:02:08.347 --> 00:02:10.727
The direct and indirect fields were highly aligned.

33
00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:14.830
So the two routes are not two maps.

34
00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:18.570
They are two reports on one spot, meeting on one neuron.

35
00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:27.850
One limit. The light silencer was validated only for gentle forces.

36
00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:30.630
So the high-force result rests on the drug.

37
00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.800
And that drug is not specific to PSDC neurons.

38
00:02:35.883 --> 00:02:40.083
And strong firing at high force is not by itself evidence of pain.

39
00:02:40.923 --> 00:02:44.603
In awake mice, the high-force press evoked no pain-related behaviour.

40
00:02:45.783 --> 00:02:48.663
The takeaway: fast timing rides the direct route.

41
00:02:49.583 --> 00:02:51.623
Sustained pressure rides the indirect one.

42
00:02:52.563 --> 00:02:55.463
Gentle touch uses both, and both report the same skin.
